# How the regression step runs a regression(), against a fake Icarus Verilog
# (fake_bin/, which the tests put on PATH), which appends each command line
# of a compilation and of a simulation to $FAKE_SIM_LOG and fails a
# simulation given +FAIL. With
# BAKE_TEST_OWN_FLOW set, the regressions run through the project's own
# flow, flows/serial.

import os

from bake import block, flow, regression, test

block(name="dut", top="sample", rtl_files=["../rtl/sample.v"])
test(name="good", target="dut", vrf_files=["../rtl/sample_tb.v"], default_sim="icarus")
test(name="bad", target="dut", vrf_files=["../rtl/sample_tb.v"], default_sim="icarus",
     vrf_runtime_options={"icarus": ["+FAIL"]})

regression(name="smoke", target="dut", tests={"good": 2})
regression(name="full", target="dut", tests={"bad": [7]}, includes=["smoke"],
           options=["vrf.runtime_options=+NIGHTLY"])

flow(name="serial_regression", dir="flows/serial")

if os.environ.get("BAKE_TEST_OWN_FLOW"):
    config.regression.flow = "serial_regression"
